Task 1: Creating Users and Groups Using CLI
Subtask 1.1: Verify FreeIPA Service Status
First, let's ensure that FreeIPA services are running properly.

Connect to your FreeIPA server via SSH or terminal
Check FreeIPA service status:
sudo systemctl status ipa
Verify you can authenticate as admin:
kinit admin
Enter the admin password when prompted.

Confirm your Kerberos ticket:
klist
Subtask 1.2: Create Groups Using ipa group-add
Groups should typically be created before users to establish proper organizational structure.

Create a basic group:
ipa group-add developers --desc="Software Development Team"
Create additional groups for different departments:
ipa group-add marketing --desc="Marketing Department"
ipa group-add hr --desc="Human Resources Department"
ipa group-add finance --desc="Finance Department"
Create a group with specific GID (Group ID):
ipa group-add contractors --desc="External Contractors" --gid=5000
Verify groups were created:
ipa group-find
Subtask 1.3: Create Users Using ipa user-add
Now let's create users and assign them to appropriate groups.

Create a basic user:
ipa user-add jsmith --first=John --last=Smith --email=jsmith@company.com
Create a user with additional attributes:
ipa user-add mjohnson --first=Mary --last=Johnson --email=mjohnson@company.com --title="Senior Developer" --phone="555-0123"
Create a user with specific UID and shell:
ipa user-add bwilson --first=Bob --last=Wilson --email=bwilson@company.com --uid=2001 --shell=/bin/bash
Create users for different departments:
ipa user-add agarcia --first=Ana --last=Garcia --email=agarcia@company.com --title="Marketing Manager"
ipa user-add dlee --first=David --last=Lee --email=dlee@company.com --title="HR Specialist"
Set initial passwords for users:
ipa passwd jsmith
ipa passwd mjohnson
ipa passwd bwilson
ipa passwd agarcia
ipa passwd dlee
Add users to groups:
ipa group-add-member developers --users=jsmith,mjohnson,bwilson
ipa group-add-member marketing --users=agarcia
ipa group-add-member hr --users=dlee
Verify user creation:
ipa user-find
Task 2: Modifying User and Group Attributes
Subtask 2.1: Modify User Attributes Using ipa user-mod
Update user's job title:
ipa user-mod jsmith --title="Lead Developer"
Change user's phone number:
ipa user-mod mjohnson --phone="555-0456"
Update user's manager:
ipa user-mod bwilson --manager=jsmith
Add additional email address:
ipa user-mod agarcia --addattr=mail=ana.garcia@company.com
Change user's home directory:
ipa user-mod dlee --homedir=/home/custom/dlee
Disable a user account temporarily:
ipa user-disable bwilson
Re-enable the user account:
ipa user-enable bwilson
View detailed user information:
ipa user-show jsmith --all
Subtask 2.2: Modify Group Attributes Using ipa group-mod
Update group description:
ipa group-mod developers --desc="Software Development and Engineering Team"
Add users to existing group:
ipa group-add-member finance --users=dlee
Remove users from group:
ipa group-remove-member hr --users=dlee
Add a group as a member of another group (nested groups):
ipa group-add-member developers --groups=contractors
View detailed group information:
ipa group-show developers --all
List all members of a group:
ipa group-show developers
