Task 4: Deleting Users and Groups
Subtask 4.1: Safe Deletion Practices
Before deleting users or groups, it's important to follow proper procedures.

Check user's group memberships:
ipa user-show bwilson --all | grep "Member of groups"
Check if user owns any resources:
ipa user-show bwilson --all
Remove user from all groups first (optional, but recommended):
ipa group-remove-member developers --users=bwilson
Subtask 4.2: Delete Users Using CLI
Delete a user account:
ipa user-del bwilson
Delete multiple users at once:
ipa user-del agarcia dlee
Verify user deletion:
ipa user-find bwilson
Subtask 4.3: Delete Groups Using CLI
Check group membership before deletion:
ipa group-show contractors
Delete an empty group:
ipa group-del contractors
Delete a group with members (this will remove the group but not the users):
ipa group-del marketing
Verify group deletion:
ipa group-find marketing
Subtask 4.4: Delete Users and Groups via Web UI
Delete users via Web UI:

Navigate to Identity → Users
Select the checkbox next to the user(s) you want to delete
Click "Delete" button
Confirm the deletion
Delete groups via Web UI:

Navigate to Identity → Groups
Select the checkbox next to the group(s) you want to delete
Click "Delete" button
Confirm the deletion
Advanced Operations
Bulk User Creation
For creating multiple users efficiently, you can use a script:

#!/bin/bash
# bulk_user_creation.sh

users=(
    "tsmith:Tom:Smith:tsmith@company.com"
    "jdoe:Jane:Doe:jdoe@company.com"
    "mwilson:Mike:Wilson:mwilson@company.com"
)

for user_info in "${users[@]}"; do
    IFS=':' read -r username firstname lastname email <<< "$user_info"
    ipa user-add "$username" --first="$firstname" --last="$lastname" --email="$email"
    echo "Created user: $username"
done
