Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Permission Denied Errors
Problem: Getting permission denied when trying to create users or groups.

Solution:

# Ensure you have valid Kerberos ticket
kinit admin
klist

# Check if you have proper admin privileges
ipa user-show admin
Issue 2: User Already Exists Error
Problem: Trying to create a user that already exists.

Solution:

# Check if user exists
ipa user-find username

# If user exists but is deleted, you may need to use --force
ipa user-add username --force
Issue 3: Group Membership Issues
Problem: Cannot add user to group or remove user from group.

Solution:

# Verify both user and group exist
ipa user-show username
ipa group-show groupname

# Check current group memberships
ipa user-show username --all | grep "Member of groups"
Issue 4: Web UI Access Problems
Problem: Cannot access FreeIPA Web UI.

Solution:

Check if httpd service is running:
sudo systemctl status httpd
Verify firewall settings:
sudo firewall-cmd --list-services
Check certificate validity and browser settings
